    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering API Integration**\n\nI'm currently focused on how to integrate with an external LLM, realizing that direct API interaction isn't feasible with existing tools. I need to select a concrete provider, and I'm figuring out how to make that provider clearly identifiable within the `extract_json.py` script.\n\n\n**Choosing OpenAI Implementation**\n\nI've decided to move forward with OpenAI as the hosted LLM provider. The code will reflect this choice directly. The `extract_json.py` script will have a function that calls the OpenAI API, taking text and returning JSON. I'll include placeholders in the code for the API key and model name, so the user can easily configure these parameters.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818878134,
          "start": 1789818875613
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b984aedd001KhHMDhOc91Foqy",
      "message_id": "msg_0b984a724001TMgjGpwBiRn6ME",
      "session_id": "ses_f467b58ebffetUVkyZw1R2suY4",
      "time_created": 1789818875613,
      "time_updated": 1789818878134
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "JbQXSHq0iOuOnFIN",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\nimport json\nimport os\n\ndef extract_json_from_text(text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (OpenAI GPT-3.5-turbo) to extract structured JSON from text.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The input text from which to extract JSON.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary representing the extracted JSON.\n    \"\"\"\n    openai.api_key = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\n\n    if not openai.api_key:\n        raise ValueError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set.\")\n\n    messages = [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant that extracts JSON objects from text.\"},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": f\"Extract the JSON object from the following text:\n\n{text}\n\nReturn only the JSON object.\"}\n    ]\n\n    try:\n        response = openai.chat.completions.create(\n            model=\"gpt-3.5-turbo\",  # Provider-specific model identifier\n            messages=messages,\n            response_format={\"type\": \"json_object\"},\n            temperature=0.0\n        )\n        json_string = response.choices[0].message.content\n        return json.loads(json_string)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error extracting JSON: {e}\")\n        return {}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    example_text = \"\"\"\n    Here is some information about a person:\n    {\n      \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n      \"age\": 30,\n      \"city\": \"New York\"\n    }\n    Please process this data.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted_data = extract_json_from_text(example_text)\n    print(\"Extracted JSON:\", extracted_data)\n\n    example_text_2 = \"No JSON here, just some plain text.\"\n    extracted_data_2 = extract_json_from_text(example_text_2)\n    print(\"Extracted JSON (should be empty):\", extracted_data_2)\n",
            "filePath": "extract_json.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-whjjkrvf/extract_json.py",
            "truncated": false
